{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-809785a6-213f-492a-a840-7174ffcdd865-1787968074741", :event/time "2026-08-29T01:47:54.741Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "809785a6-213f-492a-a840-7174ffcdd865", :text "Archaeology anchors: Knoxx/Sol currently composes role prompts, then actor prompts, then agent prompts with blank-line templates; roles also contribute capabilities/tools. Mindfuck separates immutable doctrine and a priority-ordered skill graph, while Muse only has idempotent string-section replacement. Implement the smallest pure fragment law/compiler: explicit scope, contributor kind/id, precedence/order, conditions, authority claim, EvidenceRef provenance, target set, version, deterministic conflict/budget diagnostics, and a content-free rendered receipt.", :source "agent", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1787968074739-0.8axu9lt5aqqgnh5iauy", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "7f4891c1-691f-4803-a690-450e8d49e558"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-4a15f000-ec82-482b-98c0-70d56a24b976-1787968075176", :event/time "2026-08-29T01:47:55.176Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "4a15f000-ec82-482b-98c0-70d56a24b976", :text "Depends on typed prompt fragments. Axxium, not Muse, resolves contributor identity and whether a fragment may occupy/override a prompt slot. Define signed/versioned authority decisions and reject ambiguous or multiple owners.", :source "agent", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1787968075175-0.c5rmki97oce9bz21zfx", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "0832add0-b54b-42ff-a3dc-6899425dcaba"}
